  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted ([Cover Letter], [Transport Statement], [Statement of Purpose, Mission, Vision and Long-Term Plan], [Training Plan - Sample], [105], [1749-BG-ZZ-00-DR-A-00.101], [1749-BG-ZZ-00-DR-A-10.201], Received: 11/04/2022, [Appendix C, Rev B], [Employment Assessment & Marketing Evidence Report], [The Wireless Factory and Boom Box Enquires Schedule 16/10/2019 - 27/04/2022]. [HTML Marketing Samples], [Wireless Factory Postcard - March 2018], [Wireless Factory Postcard - August 2021], [Wireless Factory Postcard - April 2022], Received: 26/05/2022, [1749-BG-ZZ-00-DR-A-20.201], [Fire Safety Strategy], Received: 06/07/2022) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 3 - No development (except any demolition, site clearance, ground investigation and remediation work) shall take place until full details (including manufacturers specifications) of secure covered cycle parking facilities (for not less than 4 bicycles) for the occupants of, and visitors to, the development have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The approved facilities shall be fully implemented and made available for use before the development is first occupied or brought into use and thereafter retained for use at all times without obstruction.",
    "Condition : 4 - No development above ground level shall take place until full details of the Electric Vehicle Charging Points, each capable of  a minimum output of 7.2kW, are submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The details shall include manufacturer's specifications and the number of spaces provided with active and passive capabilities shall comply with the London Plan standards.\r\n\r\nThe charging points shall be installed in accordance with the approved details, with photographic evidence submitted to the Local Planning Authority upon completion, and so maintained at all times thereafter.\r\n",
    "Condition : 5 - No development shall take place until a scheme for protecting the approved development from noise associated with the surrounding industrial properties within the Locally Significant Industrial Site has been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. The approved scheme shall be completed before the development is first occupied or brought into use and be retained as such thereafter."
  ],
